# Architecture Rules (full doc: docs/architecture.md)

## Layer Flow

```
UI → Controllers → Application → Services → Models
Coordinators → Controllers     ↓              ↓
               ↓             Pipes          Database
               Stores
```

## Hard Constraints

- Controllers NEVER call Services directly — go through Application
- Coordinators NEVER call Application — go through Controllers
- Application NEVER accesses Stores — only Controllers manage stores
- Pipes are pure — NO IO
- Only PostApplication, UserApplication, NotificationApplication may call other Applications (max depth 1, no cycles)

## Anti-Patterns to Catch

- Controller importing from services (must go through Application)
- Application using `useXxxStore.getState()` (stores belong to Controllers)
- Coordinator calling Application directly (must go through Controllers)
- IO inside pipes (pipes must be pure functions)
- Circular Application → Application dependencies or depth > 1

For full layer diagram, cross-domain rules, IO boundaries, and code examples: read docs/architecture.md
